From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_pas: rebuild the attach-only GLINK edge across hibernate

X1E at EL2 attaches to DSPs the bootloader started, and the EL1
hibernation notifier deliberately skips those RPROC_ATTACHED processors
because Linux cannot restart them. After a cross-boot resume the restored
GLINK channels and SMEM pointers describe the previous firmware instance,
while GLINK's IRQF_NO_SUSPEND interrupt feeds the new firmware's messages
straight into them: duplicate remote CIDs, intent timeouts, dead battery
and audio. The image-loading initramfs carries neither the PAS driver nor
the GLINK modules, so what the restored kernel needs is the same fresh
host connection a cold boot makes -- not another DSP reset. The
bridge-only PAS restart experiment failed on both DSPs with APPS force
stop and a start timeout; do not reuse it here.

Release the edge at PM_HIBERNATION_PREPARE, register it again after the
image is restored.

The side it is released on is the whole point. Removing the edge removes
its rpmsg children, and the audio one pulls the entire q6prm consumer
tree with it: apr_remove() joins the PDR notifier worker, which is in
apr_pd_status(DOWN) unregistering q6prm, whose five active managed device
links go to the LPASS macro codecs -- wsa2, rx, tx, wsa, va -- with the
SoundWire masters and the sound card behind them.
device_links_unbind_consumers() then releases each of those, and
__device_release_driver() runtime-resumes every suspended macro on the
way down.

Done on the restore side that runs against the DSP the bootloader just
started, so those clocks are unreachable. SDAM instrumentation caught it
at exactly one point: an ACTIVE link selected, the consumer referenced,
the links lock dropped, and device_release_driver_internal() never
returning, on one of those codecs. No console, no shell, no dmesg -- the
machine reset ~30 s later and took the evidence with it.

At PM_HIBERNATION_PREPARE the DSP is still the one this image has been
talking to, GPR still answers, and the notifier runs before
freeze_processes(), so userspace can still close its ALSA files. That is
the same teardown the SSR path takes, which 0099-0104 already made
survivable, and it needs SYSTEMD_SLEEP_FREEZE_USER_SESSIONS=0 so systemd
has not frozen the session before snd_card_disconnect_sync() waits on it.
The image then holds no bound LPASS macros, device_links_busy(q6prm) is
false on the restore side, and nothing is left to unbind where it cannot
survive being unbound.

POST keeps only the register half, which is fast -- the channel opens and
the rebind happen asynchronously after it -- and runs from an ordered
workqueue rather than inside hibernate(). The PM notifier executes under
system_transition_mutex with the console already restored away, so
anything that blocks there is unrecoverable; off the sleep path a stall
costs audio and leaves a machine that can be read. One queue for every
instance, not one per device: per-device queues would let the ADSP and
CDSP rebuilds run concurrently where the notifier chain ran them in
sequence. A new transition is refused while a rebuild is still running
rather than flush_work()ed, because that wait would run under the sleep
lock too.

The freeze/abort machinery stays as the fallback for a device not torn
down at entry: freeze_late masks RX and blocks TX after the children have
suspended, rejecting an active control-message worker with -EBUSY rather
than unregistering devices inside the PM traversal; restore_early leaves
RX masked and aborts senders before child resume, so removing old
endpoints cannot issue CLOSE or service shutdown into the new connection.
qcom_glink_tx() rechecks abort after every wake -- the old loop could wake
on teardown, see newly available space, and write anyway. It disengages by
itself once the edge is gone at entry.

hibernate_glink_async=n puts the rebuild back inside the POST notifier
chain, where a failure stops the chain instead of outliving it; that is
what an instrumentation round or a bisect wants. Only
PM_HIBERNATION_PREPARE tears down -- PM_RESTORE_PREPARE belongs to a
kernel whose edge is discarded when the image loads. Rollback is free: a
failing later notifier delivers PM_POST_HIBERNATION, which registers
again. EL1 is untouched, its PREPARE branch needing RPROC_RUNNING where
this one needs RPROC_ATTACHED. rproc_detach/shutdown, sysmon shutdown, SSR
cleanup and PAS reset are all avoided: the DSP stays attached.

The four dev_info lines naming each rebuild stage are deliberate. They are
what this path was debugged through once it stopped taking the machine
down, and they distinguish a rebuild that ran from one that was skipped.

Verified on hardware 2026-09-15: eight consecutive hibernate cycles, four
on battery and four on AC with the GPU pinned power/control=on so both
restore paths ran, then both DSPs attached, card0 present, all five LPASS
macros rebound and all five q6prm links re-established. Audio, battery and
USB-C glink go down at hibernate entry rather than surviving into the
image; that is the design. A same-boot test_resume does not reset the peer
and is not covered.
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include <linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h>
 #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/remoteproc.h>
+#include <linux/rpmsg/qcom_glink.h>
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.h>
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/smem.h>
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/smem_state.h>
@@ -121,6 +122,10 @@
 
 	struct notifier_block pm_notifier;
 	bool hibernate_restart;
+	bool hibernate_glink_frozen;
+	bool hibernate_glink_restore;
+	struct work_struct hibernate_glink_work;
+	bool hibernate_glink_torn;
 };
 
 static void qcom_pas_segment_dump(struct rproc *rproc,
@@ -780,6 +785,25 @@
 		 "Stop the remote processor before the hibernation image is taken and boot it again on restore (default: y)");
 
 /*
+ * Shared by every instance on purpose: a queue per device would let the ADSP
+ * and CDSP rebuilds run at once, where the notifier chain ran them in sequence.
+ */
+static struct workqueue_struct *qcom_pas_hib_wq;
+
+/*
+ * The restore-side rebuild removes every rpmsg child of the edge, and the audio
+ * one drags the whole q6prm consumer tree with it. Run from the PM notifier
+ * that happens inside hibernate(), under system_transition_mutex and with the
+ * console already gone, so anything that blocks there is unrecoverable: no log,
+ * no shell, watchdog reset. Off the sleep path a stall costs audio and leaves a
+ * machine that can be read.
+ */
+static bool qcom_pas_hibernate_glink_async = true;
+module_param_named(hibernate_glink_async, qcom_pas_hibernate_glink_async, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(hibernate_glink_async,
+		 "Rebuild the attach-only GLINK edge from a workqueue after hibernate() returns instead of inside it (default: y)");
+
+/*
  * Hibernation: take the remote processor down before the image is written and
  * boot it again afterwards.
  *
@@ -829,6 +853,179 @@
 	return ready && !stop && !fatal;
 }
 
+/* Only attach-only X1E DSPs need a host-side GLINK rebuild on restore. */
+static int __maybe_unused qcom_pas_glink_freeze_late(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_pas *pas = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	struct rproc *rproc;
+	int ret = 0;
+
+	if (!pas->rproc || !qcom_pas_hibernate_restart)
+		return 0;
+	if (!of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "qcom,x1e80100-adsp-pas") &&
+	    !of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "qcom,x1e80100-cdsp-pas"))
+		return 0;
+
+	rproc = pas->rproc;
+	mutex_lock(&rproc->lock);
+	if (!rproc->ops->start && rproc->state == RPROC_ATTACHED &&
+	    !IS_ERR_OR_NULL(pas->glink_subdev.edge)) {
+		ret = qcom_glink_smem_freeze(pas->glink_subdev.edge);
+		if (!ret)
+			pas->hibernate_glink_frozen = true;
+		else
+			dev_err(dev, "hibernate: GLINK freeze failed: %d\n", ret);
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&rproc->lock);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static int __maybe_unused qcom_pas_glink_thaw_early(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_pas *pas = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (!pas->rproc)
+		return 0;
+
+	mutex_lock(&pas->rproc->lock);
+	if (pas->hibernate_glink_frozen) {
+		if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(pas->glink_subdev.edge))
+			qcom_glink_smem_thaw(pas->glink_subdev.edge);
+		pas->hibernate_glink_frozen = false;
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&pas->rproc->lock);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int __maybe_unused qcom_pas_glink_restore_early(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_pas *pas = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (!pas->rproc)
+		return 0;
+
+	mutex_lock(&pas->rproc->lock);
+	if (pas->hibernate_glink_frozen &&
+	    !IS_ERR_OR_NULL(pas->glink_subdev.edge)) {
+		/*
+		 * Leave RX disabled. The bootloader restarted the DSP, so neither
+		 * saved channels nor cached SMEM addresses may be used again.
+		 * Abort senders before the child devices' resume callbacks run.
+		 */
+		qcom_glink_smem_abort(pas->glink_subdev.edge);
+		pas->hibernate_glink_restore = true;
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&pas->rproc->lock);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct dev_pm_ops qcom_pas_pm_ops = {
+	.freeze_late = qcom_pas_glink_freeze_late,
+	.thaw_early = qcom_pas_glink_thaw_early,
+	.restore_early = qcom_pas_glink_restore_early,
+};
+
+/*
+ * Release the attach-only edge before the snapshot rather than after it.
+ *
+ * Removing the edge removes its rpmsg children, and the audio one pulls the
+ * whole q6prm consumer tree with it: five LPASS macro codecs, two SoundWire
+ * masters, the sound card. On the restore side that runs against the DSP the
+ * bootloader just started, so the macros' clocks are unreachable -- it stopped
+ * in device_release_driver_internal() on one of those codecs and did not come
+ * back.
+ *
+ * Here the DSP is still the one this image has been talking to, GPR still
+ * answers, and PM_HIBERNATION_PREPARE runs before freeze_processes(), so
+ * userspace can still close its ALSA files. That makes this the same teardown
+ * the SSR path takes, which 0099-0104 already made survivable -- and a stall
+ * here leaves a live machine with a shell and a journal.
+ */
+static void qcom_pas_glink_teardown(struct qcom_pas *pas)
+{
+	struct qcom_rproc_glink *glink = &pas->glink_subdev;
+	struct rproc *rproc = pas->rproc;
+
+	if (!rproc || !qcom_pas_hibernate_restart)
+		return;
+	if (!of_device_is_compatible(pas->dev->of_node, "qcom,x1e80100-adsp-pas") &&
+	    !of_device_is_compatible(pas->dev->of_node, "qcom,x1e80100-cdsp-pas"))
+		return;
+
+	mutex_lock(&rproc->lock);
+	if (!rproc->ops->start && rproc->state == RPROC_ATTACHED &&
+	    !IS_ERR_OR_NULL(glink->edge)) {
+		dev_info(pas->dev, "hibernate: releasing GLINK before the image\n");
+		qcom_glink_smem_unregister(glink->edge);
+		glink->edge = NULL;
+		pas->hibernate_glink_torn = true;
+		dev_info(pas->dev, "hibernate: GLINK released\n");
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&rproc->lock);
+}
+
+static void qcom_pas_glink_restore(struct qcom_pas *pas)
+{
+	struct qcom_rproc_glink *glink = &pas->glink_subdev;
+	struct qcom_glink_smem *edge;
+	struct rproc *rproc = pas->rproc;
+	bool torn;
+
+	dev_info(pas->dev, "hibernate: GLINK rebuild enter, waiting for rproc lock\n");
+
+	/* Serialize with sysfs stop and recovery, as the rproc core does. */
+	mutex_lock(&rproc->lock);
+	pas->hibernate_glink_restore = false;
+	pas->hibernate_glink_frozen = false;
+	torn = pas->hibernate_glink_torn;
+	pas->hibernate_glink_torn = false;
+	/* A torn edge is NULL by construction; only the register half is left. */
+	if (rproc->state != RPROC_ATTACHED ||
+	    (!torn && IS_ERR_OR_NULL(glink->edge))) {
+		dev_warn(pas->dev, "hibernate: GLINK rebuild skipped: state=%d edge_error=%ld\n",
+			 rproc->state, IS_ERR(glink->edge) ? PTR_ERR(glink->edge) : 0L);
+		goto unlock;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The PM notifier runs after dpm_complete() and thaw_processes().
+	 * Removing rpmsg children here is safe; doing it from .restore
+	 * would modify the device list during the PM core's traversal.
+	 *
+	 * Do not use rproc_detach()/shutdown(): sysmon would ask the DSP
+	 * to stop, and attach-only operations cannot start it again.
+	 * TX was aborted before resume, so removing the old endpoints
+	 * cannot send CLOSE or service teardown requests to the new DSP.
+	 */
+	if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(glink->edge)) {
+		dev_info(pas->dev, "hibernate: GLINK rebuild unregister start\n");
+		qcom_glink_smem_unregister(glink->edge);
+		glink->edge = NULL;
+	}
+	dev_info(pas->dev, "hibernate: GLINK register start\n");
+	edge = qcom_glink_smem_register(glink->dev, glink->node);
+	if (IS_ERR(edge)) {
+		dev_err(pas->dev, "hibernate: GLINK reconnect failed: %ld\n",
+			PTR_ERR(edge));
+		goto unlock;
+	}
+	glink->edge = edge;
+	dev_info(pas->dev, "hibernate: reconnected GLINK to boot DSP\n");
+unlock:
+	mutex_unlock(&rproc->lock);
+}
+
+static void qcom_pas_glink_restore_work(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct qcom_pas *pas = container_of(work, struct qcom_pas,
+					    hibernate_glink_work);
+
+	qcom_pas_glink_restore(pas);
+}
+
 static int qcom_pas_pm_notify(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long action,
 			      void *data)
 {
@@ -837,6 +1034,31 @@
 	struct rproc *rproc = pas->rproc;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * A deferred rebuild from the previous cycle must not still be holding
+	 * the edge. Refuse the transition rather than flush_work() here: this
+	 * runs under system_transition_mutex, so waiting on a rebuild that is
+	 * already stuck would wedge the machine that deferring it kept alive.
+	 */
+	if ((action == PM_HIBERNATION_PREPARE || action == PM_RESTORE_PREPARE) &&
+	    work_busy(&pas->hibernate_glink_work)) {
+		dev_err(pas->dev, "hibernate: previous GLINK rebuild still running\n");
+		return notifier_from_errno(-EBUSY);
+	}
+
+	/* Not PM_RESTORE_PREPARE: that kernel's edge is discarded anyway. */
+	if (action == PM_HIBERNATION_PREPARE)
+		qcom_pas_glink_teardown(pas);
+
+	/* Rebuild whether the edge was released at entry or frozen into the image. */
+	if ((action == PM_POST_HIBERNATION || action == PM_POST_RESTORE) &&
+	    (pas->hibernate_glink_restore || pas->hibernate_glink_torn)) {
+		if (qcom_pas_hibernate_glink_async)
+			queue_work(qcom_pas_hib_wq, &pas->hibernate_glink_work);
+		else
+			qcom_pas_glink_restore(pas);
+	}
+
 	if (!qcom_pas_hibernate_restart)
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
 
@@ -1100,6 +1322,7 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto remove_ssr_sysmon;
 
+	INIT_WORK(&pas->hibernate_glink_work, qcom_pas_glink_restore_work);
 	pas->pm_notifier.notifier_call = qcom_pas_pm_notify;
 	ret = register_pm_notifier(&pas->pm_notifier);
 	if (ret)
@@ -1137,6 +1360,7 @@
 		return;
 
 	unregister_pm_notifier(&pas->pm_notifier);
+	cancel_work_sync(&pas->hibernate_glink_work);
 	rproc_del(pas->rproc);
 
 	qcom_q6v5_deinit(&pas->q6v5);
@@ -1916,9 +2140,31 @@
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "qcom_q6v5_pas",
 		.of_match_table = qcom_pas_of_match,
+		.pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&qcom_pas_pm_ops),
 	},
 };
 
-module_platform_driver(qcom_pas_driver);
+static int __init qcom_pas_init(void)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	qcom_pas_hib_wq = alloc_ordered_workqueue("qcom_pas_hib", 0);
+	if (!qcom_pas_hib_wq)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+
+	ret = platform_driver_register(&qcom_pas_driver);
+	if (ret)
+		destroy_workqueue(qcom_pas_hib_wq);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+module_init(qcom_pas_init);
+
+static void __exit qcom_pas_exit(void)
+{
+	platform_driver_unregister(&qcom_pas_driver);
+	destroy_workqueue(qcom_pas_hib_wq);
+}
+module_exit(qcom_pas_exit);
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Qualcomm Peripheral Authentication Service remoteproc driver");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL v2");
--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
@@ -100,6 +100,7 @@
  * @intentless:	flag to indicate that there is no intent
  * @tx_avail_notify: Waitqueue for pending tx tasks
  * @sent_read_notify: flag to check cmd sent or not
+ * @frozen:	block TX until the hibernation snapshot is thawed or restored
  * @abort_tx:	flag indicating that all tx attempts should fail
  */
 struct qcom_glink {
@@ -125,6 +126,7 @@
 	wait_queue_head_t tx_avail_notify;
 	bool sent_read_notify;
 
+	bool frozen;
 	bool abort_tx;
 
 	/*
@@ -375,23 +377,20 @@
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&glink->tx_lock, flags);
 
-	if (glink->abort_tx) {
-		ret = -EIO;
-		goto out;
-	}
-
-	while (qcom_glink_tx_avail(glink) < tlen) {
-		if (!wait) {
-			ret = -EAGAIN;
-			goto out;
-		}
-
+	for (;;) {
+		/* Recheck after every wake, before touching possibly stale SMEM. */
 		if (glink->abort_tx) {
 			ret = -EIO;
 			goto out;
 		}
+		if (!glink->frozen && qcom_glink_tx_avail(glink) >= tlen)
+			break;
+		if (!wait) {
+			ret = -EAGAIN;
+			goto out;
+		}
 
-		if (!glink->sent_read_notify) {
+		if (!glink->frozen && !glink->sent_read_notify) {
 			glink->sent_read_notify = true;
 			qcom_glink_send_read_notify(glink);
 		}
@@ -400,11 +399,14 @@
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&glink->tx_lock, flags);
 
 		wait_event_timeout(glink->tx_avail_notify,
-				   qcom_glink_tx_avail(glink) >= tlen, 10 * HZ);
+				   READ_ONCE(glink->abort_tx) ||
+				   (!READ_ONCE(glink->frozen) &&
+				    qcom_glink_tx_avail(glink) >= tlen), 10 * HZ);
 
 		spin_lock_irqsave(&glink->tx_lock, flags);
 
-		if (qcom_glink_tx_avail(glink) >= tlen)
+		if (!glink->abort_tx && !glink->frozen &&
+		    qcom_glink_tx_avail(glink) >= tlen)
 			glink->sent_read_notify = false;
 	}
 
@@ -1994,6 +1996,52 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* The transport IRQ must be disabled and synchronized by the caller. */
+int qcom_glink_native_freeze(struct qcom_glink *glink)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+
+	/* Do not run rpmsg registration/removal from a device PM callback. */
+	if (work_busy(&glink->rx_work))
+		return -EBUSY;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&glink->tx_lock, flags);
+	glink->frozen = true;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&glink->tx_lock, flags);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_glink_native_freeze);
+
+void qcom_glink_native_thaw(struct qcom_glink *glink)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&glink->tx_lock, flags);
+	glink->frozen = false;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&glink->tx_lock, flags);
+	wake_up_all(&glink->tx_avail_notify);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_glink_native_thaw);
+
+void qcom_glink_native_abort(struct qcom_glink *glink)
+{
+	struct glink_channel *channel;
+	unsigned long flags;
+	int cid;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&glink->tx_lock, flags);
+	glink->abort_tx = true;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&glink->tx_lock, flags);
+	wake_up_all(&glink->tx_avail_notify);
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&glink->idr_lock, flags);
+	idr_for_each_entry(&glink->lcids, channel, cid)
+		qcom_glink_intent_req_abort(channel);
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&glink->idr_lock, flags);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_glink_native_abort);
+
 void qcom_glink_native_remove(struct qcom_glink *glink)
 {
 	struct glink_channel *channel;
--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.h
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.h
@@ -35,6 +35,9 @@
 					   struct qcom_glink_pipe *rx,
 					   struct qcom_glink_pipe *tx,
 					   bool intentless);
+int qcom_glink_native_freeze(struct qcom_glink *glink);
+void qcom_glink_native_thaw(struct qcom_glink *glink);
+void qcom_glink_native_abort(struct qcom_glink *glink);
 void qcom_glink_native_remove(struct qcom_glink *glink);
 void qcom_glink_native_rx(struct qcom_glink *glink);
 
--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_smem.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_smem.c
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 	struct device dev;
 
 	int irq;
+	bool frozen;
 	struct qcom_glink *glink;
 
 	struct mbox_client mbox_client;
@@ -367,13 +368,52 @@
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_glink_smem_register);
 
-void qcom_glink_smem_unregister(struct qcom_glink_smem *smem)
+int qcom_glink_smem_freeze(struct qcom_glink_smem *smem)
 {
-	struct qcom_glink *glink = smem->glink;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (smem->frozen)
+		return 0;
 
 	disable_irq(smem->irq);
+	ret = qcom_glink_native_freeze(smem->glink);
+	if (ret) {
+		enable_irq(smem->irq);
+		return ret;
+	}
+	smem->frozen = true;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_glink_smem_freeze);
+
+void qcom_glink_smem_thaw(struct qcom_glink_smem *smem)
+{
+	if (!smem->frozen)
+		return;
+
+	qcom_glink_native_thaw(smem->glink);
+	smem->frozen = false;
+	enable_irq(smem->irq);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_glink_smem_thaw);
+
+void qcom_glink_smem_abort(struct qcom_glink_smem *smem)
+{
+	qcom_glink_native_abort(smem->glink);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_glink_smem_abort);
+
+void qcom_glink_smem_unregister(struct qcom_glink_smem *smem)
+{
+	/* Re-registration can fail after a hibernation restore. */
+	if (!smem)
+		return;
+
+	if (!smem->frozen)
+		disable_irq(smem->irq);
 
-	qcom_glink_native_remove(glink);
+	qcom_glink_native_remove(smem->glink);
 
 	mbox_free_channel(smem->mbox_chan);
